# Security (M01 open item 29). `make validate` fails on a workflow whose sha256
# (LF line endings) is not listed here, and on a listed file that is gone.
# Written at M01 PR 1 after the evals.yml edits of items 9 and 16. A PR that
# edits a workflow can edit this file too; nothing stops that until M02
# (infra/ruleset/README.md). Rewritten at M01 PR 2: deploy.yml is new, and
# evals.yml gained the item 18 probe and the S4/S6 CloudTrail lookups.
# Rewritten again at M01 PR 2 when deploy.yml took the BLOCK F refusal,
# and once more when evals.yml took `shell: bash` (cold review B1).
# Rewritten at M01 PR 3 when deploy.yml stopped describing AgentkeelBootstrap (item 7).
# And again when its refuse job was deleted (BLOCK F, after the read-back).
# evals.yml rewritten at M01 PR 3 for the digest match (ADR-0007, P1).
# Both rewritten after the PR 3 cold review: deploy.yml reuses an existing image (F3), evals.yml wording.
# deploy.yml rewritten at M02 PR 2: the deploy job on an arm64 runner, and the build step
# refusing any image that is not arm64 (AgentCore Runtime runs arm64 only; runs 35734541276).
# gates.yml added at M02 PR 2 (ruling-cited, two-key), and evals.yml gained GITHUB_TOKEN on
# make validate. Both were committed unlisted first (0e78ef8) so that this check refusing a
# second workflow file could be observed (open.md row 16, milestones/M02/runs/row16_second_workflow.yaml).
# From this PR, editing a workflow and this file together needs a Security ruling (ruling-cited on infra/**).
# evals.yml again at M02 PR 2, after its first run read that an Actions token is not shown bypass_actors:
# the live-ruleset compare moves to the evals job, whose own step fetches the ruleset with RULESET_TOKEN
# and hands validate a file (no PR code sees the secret; no if:); the checks job says it skips it.
# evals.yml at M02 PR 3: the evals job gains actions: read and one step that runs scripts/observe_pr.py on the
# three M02 run files, and hands make evals SEED_PRS_OBS, BYPASS_OBS and DOORS_OBS (SPEC/02 §4, §5.1); the
# RULESET_TOKEN step also fetches the rule-suites record into files, so the observer never sees the secret.
# Rewritten at M03 PR 2 when deploy.yml began to run on data/rights_table.json (S1's reader).
# Rewritten at M03 PR 2 when evals.yml began to look up seed S5's attempt (F3_5).
# Rewritten at M04 PR 2 when evals.yml began to run A-vs-A on a swap or a labelled PR (SPEC/04 §4).
# Rewritten at M04 PR 3 when evals.yml began to look up the swap PRs (f4_swaps.yaml; recorded, not gated).
# Rewritten at M05 PR 1 when evals.yml stopped looking up the swap PRs (milestones/M05/open.md row 1).
# Rewritten at M05 PR 2: evals.yml reads the attempts in the security account and archives envelopes there;
# cold-review-ruling.yml refuses a ruling for the PR that is not ruled (milestones/M05/open.md row 44).
# Rewritten at M06 PR 2: platform-check.yml added (the App's check, from main on a schedule, R2); deploy.yml
# deploys an agent from the template from main (R3) and writes the registry; evals.yml observes claim 6.
# Rewritten again at M06 PR 2 after the seat reviews: deploy.yml reads the registry before signing and
# claims a name first; evals.yml reads panel 1 in a step of its own (security-reviewer F2, F3, F7, F9, N5).
# And after the cold review: deploy.yml puts the answer before it writes the registry row, and reads a 412 as put (F8, F2).
# Rewritten at M07 PR 2 (SPEC/07 section 6; milestones/M07/rulings/pr2-security.md): platform-check.yml reads the App's grant back
# first in post, mints per repository and per named set, and takes the seeded relaxation as a dispatch input; platform-upgrade.yml,
# model-watch.yml and observe.yml added, each keyed job in its own environment on main's code; deploy.yml gains the retire jobs, the
# bundle put and the 412 repair; evals.yml observes claim 7, reads panel 2, and its archive job writes panel 2's rows.
# Rewritten at M07 PR 2 after the seat reviews: deploy.yml's retire job records nothing unless the runtime is gone (platform-architect B1); evals.yml's envelope-rows job writes panel 2's table through replay_history (cold review B1).
# Rewritten at M07 PR 3: deploy.yml's sign-agent uploads one folder, so deploy-agent finds the signed files (run 37023118799).
# Rewritten at M07 PR 3: observe.yml's header says what its keyed job now holds (tokens minted first, the key let go; security-reviewer 12 on M07 PR 2). No step changes.
